        {
          "competence": "calculer",
          "correction_answer": "$P(T) = P(M)\\,P_M(T) + P(\\overline{M})\\,P_{\\overline{M}}(T) = \\dfrac{3}{100} \\times \\dfrac{9}{10} + \\dfrac{97}{100} \\times \\dfrac{1}{25}$. $= \\dfrac{27}{1000} + \\dfrac{97}{2500} = \\dfrac{270}{10000} + \\dfrac{388}{10000} = \\dfrac{658}{10000} = \\dfrac{329}{5000}$. \\medskip",
          "correction_answer_scope": "question",
          "points": "2 pts",
          "question": "Q2",
          "statement": "Calculer $P(T)$ par la formule des probabilités totales. \\hfill\\textit{(2 pts --- calculer)}",
